From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:31:17 -0500
Subject: feat: the peek's card comes in when it opens (issue 91)

A peek over the page fades in over 160 ms, eased out, when it opens, so the
card is on screen while the page paints its first frame (motion O10). It
follows "Animate the sidebar and overlays" and the system's Reduce Motion
(motion O1); off, the card shows as it did. Closing is not animated.

Extensions reach the peek's page by its tab id (peek P24) and put their
scripts in it as in a tab's page, and while the peek shows its page is the
window's active tab to them (P26): the tabs API
announces it when it opens and when it closes, and Open as Tab attaches it;
a query for the active tab finds it in the pinned tab's place. F5, Cmd-R,
the address row's reload button and the page's own menu reload the peek,
not the pinned page under it (P25).

Why: GitHub issue 91. With no motion the card appeared in one frame once
the page had painted, which read as slower than Arc's peek. GitHub issue
102: a password manager's popup and keys filled the pinned page under a
peek, and after Open as Tab nothing until a reload; a reload reloaded the
pinned page.

Removable when: never; Stedding's own motion and peek.
